rsz: end the setup-repair sweep after a run of endpoints that commit nothing

Policy candidate from the repair-knobs campaign (ideas/repair-knobs-nihl.md),
carried while it is measured; retires TNS_END_PERCENT if it dominates.
Not upstreamed.

Endpoints are visited worst first. Once a run of violating endpoints has
committed no move, the ones behind them will not either, and the census
shows the sweep going on for hundreds of passes past that point for no
gain (riscv32i grt: 85% of 320 s after the last gain). This ends the
sweep after K consecutive violating endpoints that committed nothing;
endpoints found clean on arrival do not count. K defaults to 20 and
RSZ_YIELD_WINDOW overrides it while the value is being fitted on riscv32i
and jpeg, after which it is frozen.

Chesterton's Fence: TNS_END_PERCENT exists because visiting every endpoint
is expensive and a user could see, per design, where it stopped paying.
The rule reads the same signal at runtime. The knob is left in place and
still honoured.

